# =============================================================================
# Build context for the backend image.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole directory, so `docker build` uploads
# target/ (often hundreds of MB of stale classes and jars) and .git/ on every
# build. Since the Dockerfile now compiles from source, a stale target/ in the
# context is also a correctness risk: it is not used, but it silently bloats the
# image build and hides mistakes about which artifact is being shipped.
# =============================================================================

target/
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

*.md
!README.md

.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

.env
.env.*
# Keep the local stack definition, but never its secrets.
docker-compose.override.yml
